Not part of this repository, fetched and built at build time (recipes/fetch_gcc.sh, recipes/build_libstdcxx.sh):

- libstdc++ and libgcc from GCC 13.3.0 (https://gcc.gnu.org), copyright the Free Software Foundation, licensed
  GPL-3.0-or-later WITH the GCC Runtime Library Exception 3.1 (LICENSES/GPL-3.0.txt, LICENSES/GCC-exception-3.1.txt, taken
  from the GCC release). The recipe builds libstdc++.a from the unmodified GCC source (only its configure script is
  adjusted for the cross build, and its os/newlib directory is replaced by os/generic), and packages the compiler's own
  libgcc.a and libgcc_eh.a. The exception permits linking these runtime libraries into programs under any licence, so
  images and libraries built with them (including the LGPL ones, such as the browser engine) are not made GPL by it. The
  release is pinned by SHA-256 in gcc.lock.

The Symbian OS and Open C headers it compiles against (EPL-1.0 upstream, EPL-2.0 where Phorepoc updated them) come
from the Phorepoc core repository and are not copied here. The POSIX header overlay and the compiler wrappers are the pdk's
(tools/toolchain/openc_posix, tools/toolchain/mk_pure_wrappers.sh).

Thanks to the GCC project for libstdc++ and to the Symbian Foundation for releasing the platform.
